# TextFSM template: Juniper JunOS
# `show route protocol bgp <prefix|community|...> detail`. Shared by
# bgp.route / bgp.community / bgp.largecommunity / bgp.aspath because
# all four queries emit the same `show route … detail` block shape.
#
# Canonical block (truncated):
#   inet.0: 1000 destinations, 2000 routes (1000 active, 0 holddown, 0 hidden)
#   1.1.1.0/24 (2 entries, 1 announced)
#           *BGP    Preference: 170/-101
#                   Next hop type: Router, Next hop index: 1234
#                   Source: 10.0.0.2
#                   Next hop: 10.0.0.2 via xe-0/0/0.0, selected
#                   State: <Active Ext>
#                   Local AS: 65000 Peer AS: 65001
#                   Age: 1d 2:00:00     Metric: 0
#                   AS path: 65001 65002 I
#                   Communities: 65000:100 65000:200
#                   Large Communities: 214503:8:3607
#                   Accepted
#                   Localpref: 100
#                   Router ID: 10.0.0.2
#
# Capture strategy:
#   - The `*BGP` marker on the protocol line means "active path"
#     (JunOS's notion of best-path). We capture it via a dedicated
#     `best` Value that matches the literal `*BGP`/`BGP` token; the
#     projector's recBool() treats `*` as truthy.
#   - The trailing `I` / `E` / `?` token on the AS-path line is the
#     origin code (IGP/EGP/incomplete) and is consumed by the
#     `origin` Value capture at end-of-line.
#   - `as_path`, `communities`, and `large_communities` are
#     captured as single tokens spanning the whole list. The
#     projector's splitListToken() expands them per-entry, which
#     avoids the gotextfsm `${var}(?:\s+${var})*` last-only gotcha.
#   - The `Localpref:` line closes the block via Record. Real JunOS
#     output always emits Localpref before Router ID, so this is a
#     stable anchor.
Value Filldown prefix ([0-9a-fA-F:.]+/\d+)
Value best (\*?BGP)
Value nexthop ([0-9a-fA-F:.]+)
Value peer_ip ([0-9a-fA-F:.]+)
Value peer_asn (\d+)
Value med (\d+)
Value local_pref (\d+)
Value age (\S+(?:\s+\d{1,2}:\d{2}:\d{2})?)
Value as_path (\d+(?:\s+\d+)*)
Value origin ([IE?])
Value communities (\d+:\d+(?:\s+\d+:\d+)*)
Value large_communities (\d+:\d+:\d+(?:\s+\d+:\d+:\d+)*)

Start
  # Per-table preamble: `inet.0: ...` / `inet6.0: ...`.
  ^\S+\.0:\s+\d+\s+destinations
  # Prefix header opens a new block.
  ^${prefix}\s+\(\d+\s+entries
  # `*BGP` (active) or `BGP` (backup) protocol line.
  ^\s+${best}\s+Preference:
  ^\s+Source:\s+${peer_ip}
  ^\s+Next\s+hop:\s+${nexthop}\s+via
  ^\s+Local\s+AS:\s+\d+\s+Peer\s+AS:\s+${peer_asn}
  ^\s+Age:\s+${age}(?:\s+Metric:\s+${med})?
  ^\s+AS\s+path:\s+${as_path}\s+${origin}\s*$$
  ^\s+Communities:\s+${communities}\s*$$
  ^\s+Large\s+Communities:\s+${large_communities}\s*$$
  ^\s+Localpref:\s+${local_pref} -> Record
